    "title": "PHOTO GALLERY: Luzerne County Fair opening day - NewsBreak",
    "text": "19 hours ago Margaret, 9, and her sister, Elizabeth, 6, of the Back Mountain enjoy the Sizzler ride at the Luzerne County Fair. Fred Adams | For Times Leader The Luzerne County Fair opened on Wednesday and will run through Sunday. Hours are 4 to 11 p.m. Thursday, 4 to 11:30 p.m. Friday, 11 a.m. to 11:30 p.m. Saturday and 11 a.m. to 9:30 p.m. Sunday.\nGeneral admission is $10, senior citizens get in for $5 on Thursday, veterans and first responders can get $2 off the admission price for everyone in their family on Sunday, and anyone can get $2 off for bringing a non-perishable food donation for the local food pantry. If you’re shorter than 36 inches in height, admission is free every day.\nFor the schedule and other information, visit luzernecountyfair.com.\n—Staff Report",
